IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`
IMPORT `sgba-versions-acts`
IMPORT `sgba-i-s212-2022`

-- Tests for sgba-versions-acts.l4 and sgba-i-s212-2022.l4: the provisions that Act 55 of 2004, Act 21 of 2005, Act 15 of 2010 and S 212/2022 changed.
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the amending Act or Order and of the Revised Edition 2003 (BA1994.20030731.txt), not from what the code computed.
-- Dates: Act 55 of 2004 takes effect on 1 January 2005 and S 750/2004, which appoints that day, was first published on 17 December 2004;
-- Act 21 of 2005: 30 January 2006, S 878/2005 published 30 December 2005; Act 15 of 2010: 2 January 2011, S 776/2010 published 20 December 2010; S 212/2022: made 22 March 2022, published and in operation 25 March 2022.
-- Argument order of the selector: the list of versions; the day of the conduct; the day the law is read as at.

§ `S 212/2022 as an instrument`

#ASSERT `S 212/2022 was made on` EQUALS (Date 22 3 2022)
#ASSERT `S 212/2022 was first published on` EQUALS (Date 25 3 2022)
#ASSERT `S 212/2022 takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 25 3 2022)
#ASSERT `S 212/2022 para 2 sub-paragraph (a) of paragraph 2 of the Exemption (No. 2) Order is deleted, on` (Date 25 3 2022) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `S 212/2022 para 2 sub-paragraph (a) of paragraph 2 of the Exemption (No. 2) Order is deleted, on` (Date 24 3 2022) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `S 212/2022 para 2 sub-paragraph (a) of paragraph 2 of the Exemption (No. 2) Order is deleted, on` (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS TRUE

§ `The two days of each amendment, and the rows of each table`

-- The days the notifications were first published, and the days the amending Acts take effect.
#ASSERT `S 750/2004 was first published on` EQUALS (Date 17 12 2004)
#ASSERT `Act 55 of 2004 takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 1 1 2005)
#ASSERT `S 878/2005 was first published on` EQUALS (Date 30 12 2005)
#ASSERT `Act 21 of 2005 takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 30 1 2006)
#ASSERT `S 776/2010 was first published on` EQUALS (Date 20 12 2010)
#ASSERT `Act 15 of 2010 takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 2 1 2011)
-- The rows of the tables: the text after each amendment takes effect on the day the Act does and is published on the day the notification was.
#ASSERT `s 48 and s 48A as substituted by the Broadcasting (Amendment) Act 2004`'s `takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 1 1 2005)
#ASSERT `s 48 and s 48A as substituted by the Broadcasting (Amendment) Act 2004`'s `published on` EQUALS (Date 17 12 2004)
#ASSERT `s 35(3) as amended by the Companies (Amendment) Act 2005`'s `takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 30 1 2006)
#ASSERT `s 35(3) as amended by the Companies (Amendment) Act 2005`'s `published on` EQUALS (Date 30 12 2005)
#ASSERT `s 55 as amended by the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`'s `takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 2 1 2011)
#ASSERT `s 55 as amended by the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`'s `published on` EQUALS (Date 20 12 2010)
-- Of two versions the later published is read, whichever way round they are given; of one, that one.
GIVEN x IS A `Provision text version`
      y IS A MAYBE `Provision text version`
GIVETH A STRING
`the source of the later published of two versions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the later published of two provision text versions` x y
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "NOTHING"
    WHEN JUST v THEN v's `source`

#ASSERT `the source of the later published of two versions` `s 48 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003` (JUST `s 48 and s 48A as substituted by the Broadcasting (Amendment) Act 2004`) EQUALS "s 48 and s 48A as substituted by Act 55 of 2004, in operation 1 January 2005 by S 750/2004"
#ASSERT `the source of the later published of two versions` `s 48 and s 48A as substituted by the Broadcasting (Amendment) Act 2004` (JUST `s 48 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003`) EQUALS "s 48 and s 48A as substituted by Act 55 of 2004, in operation 1 January 2005 by S 750/2004"
#ASSERT `the source of the later published of two versions` `s 55 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003` NOTHING EQUALS "s 55 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003): no authorisation of the Public Prosecutor"
-- The 2003 wording of s 48(1) on its own: argument order, the act; in the course of any trade or business; the decoder is an unauthorised decoder.
#ASSERT `s 48(1) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, the person's act is prohibited` `import` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, the person's act is prohibited` `let for hire` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, the person's act is prohibited` `import` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, the person's act is prohibited` `import` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, the person's act is prohibited` `modify` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Act 55 of 2004, ss 48 and 48A: which text is read`

-- before the Revised Edition 2003 there is no text
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS "NOTHING"
-- a reading day before the Revised Edition 2003 was published
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` (Date 31 7 2003) (Date 30 7 2003) EQUALS "NOTHING"
-- the Revised Edition 2003, read on its own day
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` (Date 31 7 2003) (Date 31 7 2003) EQUALS "s 48 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003); there was no s 48A"
-- the day before the Act takes effect
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` (Date 31 12 2004) (Date 1 6 2005) EQUALS "s 48 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003); there was no s 48A"
-- the day the Act takes effect, read on the day S 750/2004 was first published
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` (Date 1 1 2005) (Date 17 12 2004) EQUALS "s 48 and s 48A as substituted by Act 55 of 2004, in operation 1 January 2005 by S 750/2004"
-- the same conduct day read the day before S 750/2004 was published: the Act alone does not say when it takes effect
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` (Date 1 1 2005) (Date 16 12 2004) EQUALS "s 48 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003); there was no s 48A"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` (Date 2 1 2005) (Date 16 12 2004) EQUALS "s 48 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003); there was no s 48A"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 15 9 2012) EQUALS "s 48 and s 48A as substituted by Act 55 of 2004, in operation 1 January 2005 by S 750/2004"
-- the day the sources were last checked (4 November 2026, assumed, not ruled)
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS "s 48 and s 48A as substituted by Act 55 of 2004, in operation 1 January 2005 by S 750/2004"
-- the day after it
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) EQUALS "NOTHING"

§ `Act 21 of 2005, s 35(3): which text is read`

#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 35(3) versions` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS "NOTHING"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 35(3) versions` (Date 31 7 2003) (Date 31 7 2003) EQUALS "s 35(3) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003): 5% of the nominal amount of all voting shares"
-- the day before the Act takes effect
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 35(3) versions` (Date 29 1 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) EQUALS "s 35(3) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003): 5% of the nominal amount of all voting shares"
-- the day it takes effect, read on the day S 878/2005 was first published
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 35(3) versions` (Date 30 1 2006) (Date 30 12 2005) EQUALS "s 35(3) as amended by Act 21 of 2005, in operation 30 January 2006 by S 878/2005: 5% of the total votes attached to all voting shares"
-- read the day before S 878/2005 was published
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 35(3) versions` (Date 30 1 2006) (Date 29 12 2005) EQUALS "s 35(3) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003): 5% of the nominal amount of all voting shares"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 35(3) versions` (Date 1 6 2020) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS "s 35(3) as amended by Act 21 of 2005, in operation 30 January 2006 by S 878/2005: 5% of the total votes attached to all voting shares"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 35(3) versions` (Date 1 6 2020) (Date 5 11 2026) EQUALS "NOTHING"

§ `Act 15 of 2010, s 55: which text is read`

#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 55 versions` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS "NOTHING"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 55 versions` (Date 31 7 2003) (Date 31 7 2003) EQUALS "s 55 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003): no authorisation of the Public Prosecutor"
-- the day before the Code takes effect, read now
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 55 versions` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS "s 55 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003): no authorisation of the Public Prosecutor"
-- the day it takes effect, read on the day S 776/2010 was first published
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 55 versions` (Date 2 1 2011) (Date 20 12 2010) EQUALS "s 55 as amended by Act 15 of 2010, in operation 2 January 2011 by S 776/2010: with the authorisation of the Public Prosecutor"
-- read the day before S 776/2010 was published
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 55 versions` (Date 2 1 2011) (Date 19 12 2010) EQUALS "s 55 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003): no authorisation of the Public Prosecutor"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 55 versions` (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 1 6 2012) EQUALS "s 55 as amended by Act 15 of 2010, in operation 2 January 2011 by S 776/2010: with the authorisation of the Public Prosecutor"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 55 versions` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) EQUALS "NOTHING"

§ `S 212/2022, O 2: which text is read`

-- before the Order takes effect: the earlier text of O 2 is not held
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the O 2 versions` (Date 24 3 2022) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS "NOTHING"
-- in operation but not yet published on the reading day
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the O 2 versions` (Date 25 3 2022) (Date 24 3 2022) EQUALS "NOTHING"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the O 2 versions` (Date 25 3 2022) (Date 25 3 2022) EQUALS "O 2 as amended by S 212/2022: sub-paragraph (a) of paragraph 2 deleted, in operation 25 March 2022"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the O 2 versions` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS "O 2 as amended by S 212/2022: sub-paragraph (a) of paragraph 2 deleted, in operation 25 March 2022"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the O 2 versions` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) EQUALS "NOTHING"

§ `O 2 para 2: the companies exempt from section 33, on two days`

#ASSERT `O 2 para 2 the company is exempt from section 33 of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) "STT Communications Ltd" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `O 2 para 2 the company is exempt from section 33 of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) "Temasek Holdings (Private) Limited" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `O 2 para 2 the company is exempt from section 33 of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) "Mediacorp Pte. Ltd." EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `O 2 para 2 the company is exempt from section 33 of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 25 3 2022) (Date 25 3 2022) "Singapore Technologies Pte Ltd" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `O 2 para 2 the company is exempt from section 33 of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 24 3 2022) (Date 4 11 2026) "Singapore Technologies Pte Ltd" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `O 2 para 2 the company is exempt from section 33 of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 25 3 2022) (Date 24 3 2022) "Singapore Technologies Pte Ltd" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `O 2 para 2 the company is exempt from section 33 of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) "STT Communications Ltd" EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 48(1): the prohibition, on two days`

-- Argument order: conduct day; reading day; the act; the act is done in the course of any trade or business; the decoder is an unauthorised decoder; the person knows it is.
-- Revised Edition 2003: five acts, in the course of any trade or business, no element of knowledge.
-- sold in the course of trade, knowledge not required
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2004) (Date 1 6 2004) `sell` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not in the course of any trade or business
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2004) (Date 1 6 2004) `sell` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2004) (Date 1 6 2004) `let for hire` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- export was not one of the five acts
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2004) (Date 1 6 2004) `export` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- nor was distribution
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2004) (Date 1 6 2004) `otherwise distribute` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not an unauthorised decoder
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2004) (Date 1 6 2004) `sell` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- conduct on the day the Act takes effect, read before S 750/2004 was published: the old text
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 1 2005) (Date 16 12 2004) `sell` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- before the Revised Edition 2003
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 4 11 2026) `sell` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Act 55 of 2004: the act must be done knowing the decoder is unauthorised; the course of trade is not an element
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) `export` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- without knowledge
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) `export` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not in the course of any trade or business
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) `sell` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- conduct on the day the Act takes effect, read the day S 750/2004 was published
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 1 2005) (Date 17 12 2004) `export` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) `otherwise distribute` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) `sell` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 48(3) of the Revised Edition 2003: proof of the act is evidence of knowledge`

#ASSERT `s 48(3) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, proof of the act is evidence that the person knew the decoder was an unauthorised decoder` `import` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(3) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, proof of the act is evidence that the person knew the decoder was an unauthorised decoder` `manufacture` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(3) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, proof of the act is evidence that the person knew the decoder was an unauthorised decoder` `export` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(3) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, proof of the act is evidence that the person knew the decoder was an unauthorised decoder` `sell` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 48: the punishment on conviction, and s 48A, on two days`

-- The fine is $40,000 in both texts.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the fine under s 48 on a day pair` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 48 the punishment on conviction, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `fine not exceeding`)

#ASSERT `the fine under s 48 on a day pair` (Date 1 6 2004) (Date 1 6 2004) EQUALS JUST 40000
#ASSERT `the fine under s 48 on a day pair` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) EQUALS JUST 40000
#ASSERT `the fine under s 48 on a day pair` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 1 6 2006) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 48A is new: it does not exist before 1 January 2005
#ASSERT `s 48A is part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 31 12 2004) (Date 1 6 2005) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48A is part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 1 2005) (Date 17 12 2004) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- read before S 750/2004 was published
#ASSERT `s 48A is part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 1 2005) (Date 16 12 2004) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48A is part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48A is part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 1 6 2005) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 35(3): the measure of the 5%, on two days`

-- Argument order: conduct day; reading day; the person enters on or after 2 September 2002 into an agreement; the percentage of the nominal amount; the percentage of the total votes; the person first obtained the Minister's approval.
-- before 30 January 2006 the measure is the nominal amount
#ASSERT `s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) TRUE 6 4 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) TRUE 4 6 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- exactly 5% is not more than 5%
#ASSERT `s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) TRUE 5 9 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- with the approval of the Minister
#ASSERT `s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) TRUE 6 6 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- from 30 January 2006 the measure is the total votes
#ASSERT `s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) TRUE 6 4 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) TRUE 4 6 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no agreement or arrangement
#ASSERT `s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) FALSE 4 6 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- conduct on the day the Act takes effect, read on the day S 878/2005 was published
#ASSERT `s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 30 1 2006) (Date 30 12 2005) TRUE 4 6 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- read the day before
#ASSERT `s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 30 1 2006) (Date 29 12 2005) TRUE 4 6 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- before the Revised Edition 2003
#ASSERT `s 35(3) the person has contravened the subsection, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 1 6 2006) TRUE 6 6 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 55: the authorisation of the Public Prosecutor, on two days`

-- Argument order: conduct day; reading day; the Public Prosecutor has authorised it; the person is an officer of the Authority, or an officer of the Government authorised in writing by the Chief Executive.
-- before 2 January 2011 no authorisation of the Public Prosecutor is needed
#ASSERT `s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2010) (Date 1 6 2010) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- but the person must be an officer
#ASSERT `s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2010) (Date 1 6 2010) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- from 2 January 2011 the authorisation is needed
#ASSERT `s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 1 6 2012) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 1 6 2012) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2012) (Date 1 6 2012) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- conduct on the day the Code takes effect, read on the day S 776/2010 was published
#ASSERT `s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 2 1 2011) (Date 20 12 2010) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- read the day before
#ASSERT `s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 2 1 2011) (Date 19 12 2010) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- before the Revised Edition 2003
#ASSERT `s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 1 6 2012) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
